    {"content":"<h1>How to Pass Creación Digital I</h1><h2>Universidad Europea · UEM 2026-27</h2><p><strong>Rubén Vega Balbás, PhD</strong></p><p><em>6 ECTS · 150 h · 80 h contact</em></p><p>Final event theme: <strong>Communicate and inspire: What is fashion for you?</strong></p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Official weights (guía)</h2><table><tr><th>Knowledge tests</th><td><strong>55%</strong></td><td>D5 Exam</td></tr><tr><th>Case / problem</th><td><strong>15%</strong></td><td>D3 Atrium</td></tr><tr><th>Research &amp; projects</th><td><strong>20%</strong></td><td>D1 Analysis 10% + D2 Transposition 10%</td></tr><tr><th>Lab notebook</th><td><strong>10%</strong></td><td>D4 Final Digital Portfolio Notebook</td></tr></table><p>These are the four official instruments. The work-plan deliverables make them visible; they do not add extra percentages.</p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Work-plan assessment map — total 100%</h2><table><tr><th>Deliverable</th><th>Weight</th><th>Official instrument</th></tr><tr><td><strong>D1 Live fashion-image analysis</strong></td><td><strong>10%</strong></td><td>Research &amp; projects</td></tr><tr><td><strong>D2 Transposition</strong></td><td><strong>10%</strong></td><td>Research &amp; projects</td></tr><tr><td><strong>D3 Atrium</strong></td><td><strong>15%</strong></td><td>Case / problem</td></tr><tr><td><strong>D4 Final Digital Portfolio Notebook</strong></td><td><strong>10%</strong></td><td>Lab notebook</td></tr><tr><td><strong>D5 Exam</strong></td><td><strong>55%</strong></td><td>Knowledge tests</td></tr><tr><th>Total</th><th><strong>100%</strong></th><th>Official categories preserved</th></tr></table>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Every session (order binding)</h2><ol><li><strong>Analysis strip</strong> — sessions 1–2: professor models analysis; from session 3: <strong>2 students × 15 min</strong> defence</li><li><strong>Masterclass</strong> — ideas + images</li><li><strong>Lab (Portfolio)</strong> — exercises + debates → portfolio</li><li><strong>Workshop (from session 4)</strong> — ≈ half D2 Transposition · ≈ half D3 final event</li></ol><p>Sessions 1–3: <em>no Workshop</em> — end after Lab. <em>Lab ≠ Workshop.</em></p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Slide rule</h2><p>Before Lab exercises, a <strong>geometrical</strong> slide announces: exercises are coming and they go into your <strong>portfolio index</strong>.</p><p>Workshop open + outro also use geometrical backgrounds. Masterclass content uses accepted course media packs.</p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Five deliverables</h2><ol><li><strong>D1 Analysis — 10%</strong> · 15 min defence · slideshow · fashion image related to a <strong>Madrid exhibition</strong> piece</li><li><strong>D2 Transposition — 10%</strong> · <strong>same as ACT3:</strong> cartel from another language (song, film, poem, literary work, theatre…) · image series OK · source + process trail</li><li><strong>D3 Atrium — 15%</strong> · tech script + live defence · <em>What is fashion for you?</em></li><li><strong>D4 Portfolio index — 10%</strong> · Lab exercises + D1–D3</li><li><strong>D5 Exam — 55%</strong> · critical demonstration + portfolio self-review</li></ol><p><strong>Reading rule:</strong> D1 10% + D2 10% make the official Research &amp; projects 20%; D3 is the official Case / problem 15%.</p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>D1 intra-rubric</h2><table><tr><th>Presentation</th><td>70%</td></tr><tr><th>Deliverable support</th><td>20%</td></tr><tr><th>Peer debate</th><td>10%</td></tr></table><p>Two students per session from session 3. Source files + process trail required.</p>"},
    {"content":"<h2>Dignity Day and assessment conditions</h2><p><strong>Dignity Day:</strong> 21 October 2026 · <strong>Dignity Week:</strong> Friday 23 October 2026. The activity is course learning and does not create a new assessment percentage. Binding assessment dates and procedures: official UEM guide + Campus Virtual. Teaching evidence is not research data — exhibition needs consent.</p>","calendar_note":true},
